IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `sgta-nouns`

-- INSTRUMENT: Telecommunications (Radio-communication) Regulations (Cap. 323, Rg 5), 2002 Revised Edition, regulation 2:
-- the definitions, one function each ("station" is in sgta-i-rg5-radio.l4 as well, and is repeated here only as a quotation).
-- Text: subjects/sg/telecommunications-radio-communication-regulations-2001/registers/source-bundle/TA1999-RG5.txt.
-- A definition that depends on another instrument or the Act takes the borrowed fact as an input.
-- S 461/2009 changes the definition of "class licence" and adds four definitions; see sgta-i-rg5-amendments.l4.

§ `Rg 5 regulation 2: definitions`

-- src:TA1999-RG5:195 | 2. In these Regulations, unless the context otherwise requires —
-- src:TA1999-RG5:196 | "Amateur Station" means a station in respect of which an Amateur Station
-- src:TA1999-RG5:197 | licensee is authorised in the licence to use;
-- src:TA1999-RG5:198 | "armed forces" means the Singapore Armed Forces established under the
-- src:TA1999-RG5:199 | Singapore Armed Forces Act (Cap. 295) and includes any visiting force,
-- src:TA1999-RG5:200 | not being a police force, which is lawfully present in Singapore;
-- src:TA1999-RG5:201 | "Armed Forces Communication" means radio-communication —
-- src:TA1999-RG5:202 | (a) between stations of the armed forces; or
-- src:TA1999-RG5:203 | (b) between stations of the armed forces and any other radio-
-- src:TA1999-RG5:204 | communication station, whether on shore or on any vessel or aircraft;
-- src:TA1999-RG5:205 | "authorised officer" means any officer authorised by the Authority to act on its
-- src:TA1999-RG5:206 | behalf;
-- src:TA1999-RG5:207 | "class licence" means a class licence referred to in regulation 65;
-- src:TA1999-RG5:208 | "class licensee" means a person who is deemed to have been granted a class
-- src:TA1999-RG5:209 | licence;
-- src:TA1999-RG5:210 | "interference" —
-- src:TA1999-RG5:211 | (a) in relation to radio-communication, means interference to or with
-- src:TA1999-RG5:212 | radio-communications that is attributable, whether wholly or partly and
-- src:TA1999-RG5:213 | whether directly or indirectly, to an emission of electromagnetic energy by
-- src:TA1999-RG5:214 | any device; and
-- src:TA1999-RG5:215 | (b) in relation to the uses or functions of any station, network or radio-
-- src:TA1999-RG5:216 | communication equipment, means interference to or with the uses or
-- src:TA1999-RG5:217 | functions that is attributable, whether wholly or partly and whether
-- src:TA1999-RG5:218 | directly or indirectly, to an emission of electromagnetic energy by the
-- src:TA1999-RG5:219 | station, network or radio-communication equipment;
-- src:TA1999-RG5:220 | "International Telecommunication Convention" means the Convention of the
-- src:TA1999-RG5:221 | International Telecommunication Union signed at Nairobi in 1982 or any
-- src:TA1999-RG5:222 | subsequent revision or modification thereof to which the Government of
-- src:TA1999-RG5:223 | Singapore is a party;
-- src:TA1999-RG5:224 | "licence" means a station (spectrum) licence, a network (spectrum) licence, a
-- src:TA1999-RG5:225 | station licence, a network licence or a class licence or all or any of these
-- src:TA1999-RG5:226 | licences, as the context may require;
-- src:TA1999-RG5:227 | "licensee" —
-- src:TA1999-RG5:228 | (a) in relation to a station (spectrum) licence, a network (spectrum)
-- src:TA1999-RG5:229 | licence, a station licence or a network licence, means the holder of the
-- src:TA1999-RG5:230 | licence; or
-- src:TA1999-RG5:231 | (b) in relation to a class licence, means the person deemed to have been
-- src:TA1999-RG5:232 | granted the class licence;
-- src:TA1999-RG5:233 | "localised private network" means a private network that provides radio coverage
-- src:TA1999-RG5:234 | of a confined or restricted area as specified by the Authority and that
-- src:TA1999-RG5:235 | comprises at least 2 stations each operating generally at an effective
-- src:TA1999-RG5:236 | radiated power of 5 watts or below;
-- src:TA1999-RG5:237 | "Localised Radio-communication Station" means a station that can only be used
-- src:TA1999-RG5:238 | for communication with a base station or with another station within a
-- src:TA1999-RG5:239 | defined power limit specified by the Authority;
-- src:TA1999-RG5:240 | "network" means 2 or more stations operated by a person and used or intended to
-- src:TA1999-RG5:241 | be used in communication with one another;
-- src:TA1999-RG5:242 | "network licence" means a licence referred to in regulation 28;
-- src:TA1999-RG5:243 | "network (spectrum) licence" means a licence referred to in regulation 23;
-- src:TA1999-RG5:244 | "private network" means a network which —
-- src:TA1999-RG5:245 | (a) exists to meet the exclusive internal telecommunication needs of the
-- src:TA1999-RG5:246 | licensee; or
-- src:TA1999-RG5:247 | (b) has a number of common interest groups of subscribers or users and
-- src:TA1999-RG5:248 | radio channels as the Authority may specify;
-- src:TA1999-RG5:249 | "public mobile network" means any public network that enables radio-
-- src:TA1999-RG5:250 | communications through the use of portable or mobile stations and may
-- src:TA1999-RG5:251 | include any of the following telecommunication systems licensed under
-- src:TA1999-RG5:252 | section 5 of the Act:
-- src:TA1999-RG5:253 | (a) a public cellular mobile telephone system;
-- src:TA1999-RG5:254 | (b) a public radio paging system;
-- src:TA1999-RG5:255 | (c) a public mobile data system;
-- src:TA1999-RG5:256 | (d) a public trunked radio system; or
-- src:TA1999-RG5:257 | (e) a public satellite mobile telephone or data system;
-- src:TA1999-RG5:258 | "public network" means a network which is accessible to any member of the
-- src:TA1999-RG5:259 | public generally and which is used or intended to be used to provide
-- src:TA1999-RG5:260 | telecommunication services by means of radio-communication to the
-- src:TA1999-RG5:261 | general public;
-- src:TA1999-RG5:262 | "radio frequency band" means any contiguous range of radio frequencies;
-- src:TA1999-RG5:263 | "radio frequency band plan" means a plan prepared under regulation 4;
-- src:TA1999-RG5:264 | "radio frequency spectrum" means the range of frequencies within which radio-
-- src:TA1999-RG5:265 | communications are capable of being made;
-- src:TA1999-RG5:266 | "Radio Regulations" means the Radio Regulations annexed to the International
-- src:TA1999-RG5:267 | Telecommunication Convention and includes every revision or
-- src:TA1999-RG5:268 | modification thereof which the Government has ratified or accepted;
-- src:TA1999-RG5:269 | "radio spectrum plan" means a plan prepared under regulation 3;
-- src:TA1999-RG5:270 | "reception" , in relation to any radio emission, includes interception;
-- src:TA1999-RG5:271 | "spectrum right" means a right to use any specified part of the radio frequency
-- src:TA1999-RG5:272 | spectrum granted under regulation 6 (2);
-- src:TA1999-RG5:273 | "station" means a transmitter, a receiver, a combination of transmitters and
-- src:TA1999-RG5:274 | receivers or any accessory thereto which is used or intended to be used for
-- src:TA1999-RG5:275 | radio-communication;
-- src:TA1999-RG5:276 | "station licence" means a Ship Station Licence, an Aircraft Station Licence, an
-- src:TA1999-RG5:277 | Amateur Station Licence, an Experimental Station Licence, a Localised
-- src:TA1999-RG5:278 | Radio-communication Station Licence, a General Radio-communication
-- src:TA1999-RG5:279 | Station Licence, a Satellite Communication Station Licence or a Special
-- src:TA1999-RG5:280 | Purpose Station Licence, granted under Part VI;
-- src:TA1999-RG5:281 | "station (spectrum) licence" means a licence referred to in regulation 23;
-- src:TA1999-RG5:282 | "wide-area private network" means a private network that provides radio coverage
-- src:TA1999-RG5:283 | of a wide area as specified by the Authority and that comprises one or
-- src:TA1999-RG5:284 | more stations operating generally at an effective radiated power of more
-- src:TA1999-RG5:285 | than 5 watts.
@ref Rg 5 reg 2 (src:TA1999-RG5:195-285)
GIVEN `the licensee is authorised in the licence to use it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 2: this is an "Amateur Station"` MEANS
    `the licensee is authorised in the licence to use it`

GIVEN `it is the Singapore Armed Forces established under the Singapore Armed Forces Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a visiting force, not a police force, lawfully present in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 2: this is "armed forces"` MEANS
    `it is the Singapore Armed Forces established under the Singapore Armed Forces Act` OR `it is a visiting force, not a police force, lawfully present in Singapore`

GIVEN `it is radio-communication between stations of the armed forces` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is radio-communication between a station of the armed forces and any other radio-communication station, on shore or on a vessel or aircraft` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 2: this is "Armed Forces Communication"` MEANS
    `it is radio-communication between stations of the armed forces` OR `it is radio-communication between a station of the armed forces and any other radio-communication station, on shore or on a vessel or aircraft`

GIVEN `the Authority authorised the officer to act on its behalf` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 2: this is an "authorised officer"` MEANS
    `the Authority authorised the officer to act on its behalf`

GIVEN `it is a class licence referred to in regulation 65` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 2: this is a "class licence"` MEANS
    `it is a class licence referred to in regulation 65`

GIVEN `the person is deemed to have been granted a class licence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 2: this is a "class licensee"` MEANS
    `the person is deemed to have been granted a class licence`

GIVEN `it is attributable to an emission of electromagnetic energy by a device, wholly or partly, directly or indirectly` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is interference to or with radio-communications` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is interference to or with the uses or functions of a station, network or radio-communication equipment, attributable to an emission by that station, network or equipment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 2: this is "interference"` MEANS
    ((`it is attributable to an emission of electromagnetic energy by a device, wholly or partly, directly or indirectly` AND `it is interference to or with radio-communications`)
      OR `it is interference to or with the uses or functions of a station, network or radio-communication equipment, attributable to an emission by that station, network or equipment`)

GIVEN `it is the Convention of the International Telecommunication Union signed at Nairobi in 1982, or a subsequent revision or modification to which Singapore is a party` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 2: this is the "International Telecommunication Convention"` MEANS
    `it is the Convention of the International Telecommunication Union signed at Nairobi in 1982, or a subsequent revision or modification to which Singapore is a party`

GIVEN `it is a station (spectrum) licence, a network (spectrum) licence, a station licence, a network licence or a class licence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 2: this is a "licence"` MEANS
    `it is a station (spectrum) licence, a network (spectrum) licence, a station licence, a network licence or a class licence`

GIVEN `the person holds a station (spectrum) licence, a network (spectrum) licence, a station licence or a network licence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is deemed to have been granted a class licence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 2: this is a "licensee"` MEANS
    `the person holds a station (spectrum) licence, a network (spectrum) licence, a station licence or a network licence` OR `the person is deemed to have been granted a class licence`

GIVEN `it is a private network providing radio coverage of a confined or restricted area as the Authority specified` IS A BOOLEAN
      `number of stations` IS A NUMBER
      `every station operates generally at an effective radiated power of 5 watts or below` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 2: this is a "localised private network"` MEANS
    `it is a private network providing radio coverage of a confined or restricted area as the Authority specified` AND (`number of stations` AT LEAST 2) AND `every station operates generally at an effective radiated power of 5 watts or below`

GIVEN `it can only be used for communication with a base station or with another station within a defined power limit the Authority specified` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 2: this is a "Localised Radio-communication Station"` MEANS
    `it can only be used for communication with a base station or with another station within a defined power limit the Authority specified`

GIVEN `number of stations operated by a person` IS A NUMBER
      `they are used or intended to be used in communication with one another` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 2: these stations are a "network"` MEANS
    (`number of stations operated by a person` AT LEAST 2) AND `they are used or intended to be used in communication with one another`

GIVEN `it is a licence referred to in regulation 28` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 2: this is a "network licence"` MEANS
    `it is a licence referred to in regulation 28`

GIVEN `it is a licence referred to in regulation 23` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 2: this is a "network (spectrum) licence" or a "station (spectrum) licence"` MEANS
    `it is a licence referred to in regulation 23`

GIVEN `the network exists to meet the exclusive internal telecommunication needs of the licensee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the network has a number of common interest groups of subscribers or users and radio channels as the Authority specified` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 2: this is a "private network"` MEANS
    `the network exists to meet the exclusive internal telecommunication needs of the licensee` OR `the network has a number of common interest groups of subscribers or users and radio channels as the Authority specified`

GIVEN `it is a public network that enables radio-communications through portable or mobile stations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a public cellular mobile telephone system, a public radio paging system, a public mobile data system, a public trunked radio system or a public satellite mobile telephone or data system licensed under section 5 of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 2: this is a "public mobile network"` MEANS
    `it is a public network that enables radio-communications through portable or mobile stations`
    AND `it is a public cellular mobile telephone system, a public radio paging system, a public mobile data system, a public trunked radio system or a public satellite mobile telephone or data system licensed under section 5 of the Act`

GIVEN `it is accessible to any member of the public generally` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is used or intended to be used to provide telecommunication services by radio-communication to the general public` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 2: this is a "public network"` MEANS
    `it is accessible to any member of the public generally` AND `it is used or intended to be used to provide telecommunication services by radio-communication to the general public`

GIVEN `it is a contiguous range of radio frequencies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 2: this is a "radio frequency band"` MEANS
    `it is a contiguous range of radio frequencies`

GIVEN `it is a plan prepared under regulation 4` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 2: this is a "radio frequency band plan"` MEANS
    `it is a plan prepared under regulation 4`

GIVEN `it is the range of frequencies within which radio-communications are capable of being made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 2: this is the "radio frequency spectrum"` MEANS
    `it is the range of frequencies within which radio-communications are capable of being made`

GIVEN `they are the Radio Regulations annexed to the International Telecommunication Convention` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a revision or modification of them has been ratified or accepted by the Government` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 2: these are the "Radio Regulations"` MEANS
    `they are the Radio Regulations annexed to the International Telecommunication Convention` OR `a revision or modification of them has been ratified or accepted by the Government`

GIVEN `it is a plan prepared under regulation 3` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 2: this is a "radio spectrum plan"` MEANS
    `it is a plan prepared under regulation 3`

GIVEN `it is reception of a radio emission` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is interception of a radio emission` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 2: this is "reception"` MEANS
    `it is reception of a radio emission` OR `it is interception of a radio emission`

GIVEN `it is a right to use a specified part of the radio frequency spectrum granted under regulation 6(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 2: this is a "spectrum right"` MEANS
    `it is a right to use a specified part of the radio frequency spectrum granted under regulation 6(2)`

GIVEN `type of licence` IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 2: this is a "station licence" granted under Part VI` MEANS
    elem `type of licence` (LIST "Ship Station Licence", "Aircraft Station Licence", "Amateur Station Licence", "Experimental Station Licence"
                              , "Localised Radio-communication Station Licence", "General Radio-communication Station Licence"
                              , "Satellite Communication Station Licence", "Special Purpose Station Licence")

GIVEN `it is a private network providing radio coverage of a wide area as the Authority specified` IS A BOOLEAN
      `number of stations` IS A NUMBER
      `the stations operate generally at an effective radiated power of more than 5 watts` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 2: this is a "wide-area private network"` MEANS
    `it is a private network providing radio coverage of a wide area as the Authority specified` AND (`number of stations` AT LEAST 1) AND `the stations operate generally at an effective radiated power of more than 5 watts`
